  <KnownIssues>
    <Issue id="KI-001" component="fastembed/ort" version="5.13.4/2.0.0-rc.12">
      <Description>First embedding use may download ONNX model assets and ONNX Runtime binaries into the configured cache directory.</Description>
      <Workaround>Embeddings are disabled by default for release-safe installs; enable with syn config set embedding.enabled true when local model downloads are acceptable. Indexing and search fall back to lexical behavior on provider failure.</Workaround>
    </Issue>
    <Issue id="KI-002" component="fastembed/tokenizers/paste" version="5.13.4/0.22.2/1.0.15">
      <Description>cargo audit reports RUSTSEC-2024-0436 because tokenizers depends on the unmaintained paste crate through fastembed 5.13.4. fastembed is currently the latest available release and the advisory is a maintenance warning, not a vulnerability.</Description>
      <Workaround>CI runs cargo audit --deny warnings with an explicit RUSTSEC-2024-0436 waiver until fastembed releases a tokenizers line that removes paste or Synapse replaces the embedding provider.</Workaround>
    </Issue>
    <Issue id="KI-003" component="ort/x86_64-apple-darwin" version="2.0.0-rc.12">
      <Description>ort does not publish a prebuilt ONNX Runtime binary for the hosted x86_64-apple-darwin target used by the v2.6.2 release workflow.</Description>
      <Workaround>v2.6.2 publishes prebuilt artifacts for Linux x86_64, Linux aarch64, and macOS arm64 only. macOS Intel packaging remains deferred until the ONNX Runtime dependency has a compatible hosted release path or Synapse ships a separate build strategy.</Workaround>
    </Issue>
  </KnownIssues>
